meta {
  name: List curricula for this class
  type: http
  seq: 19
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/curricula?academic_session_id={{sessionId}}&subject_id={{subjectId}}&grade_level_id={{gradeLevelId}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.count: eq 1
  res.body.curricula[0].id: eq {{curriculumId}}
}

docs {
  The three filters that identify a class's syllabus, which is also the tuple
  the one-active rule is enforced on. Asking this question with a status=active
  filter is how a timetable finds the syllabus it should be teaching from.

  Newest first, as everywhere else. A draft written today is what somebody is
  working on; last year's archived copy is not what they want at the top.
}
